              This option sets the source IP address of the query. The aaddddrreessss
              must be a valid address on one of the host's network interfaces,
              or "0.0.0.0" or "::". An optional port may be specified  by  ap‐
              pending ##ppoorrtt.

       --cc ccllaassss
              This option sets the query class. The default ccllaassss is IN; other
              classes are HS for Hesiod records or CH for Chaosnet records.

       --ff ffiillee
              This option sets batch mode, in which ddiigg reads a list of lookup
              requests  to  process from the given ffiillee. Each line in the file
              should be organized in the same way it would be presented  as  a
              query to ddiigg using the command-line interface.

       --hh     Print a usage summary.

       --kk kkeeyyffiillee
