              dresses to names. The aaddddrr is an IPv4 address in  dotted-decimal
              notation,  or a colon-delimited IPv6 address. When the _-_x option
              is used, there is no need to provide the nnaammee, ccllaassss,  and  ttyyppee
              arguments.   ddiigg automatically performs a lookup for a name like
              9944..22..00..119922..iinn--aaddddrr..aarrppaa and sets the query type and class to PTR
              and IN respectively. IPv6 addresses are looked up  using  nibble
              format under the IP6.ARPA domain.

